==English==
{{wikipedia}}
{{slim-wikipedia|Bolivia, North Carolina}}

===Etymology===
{{bor+|en|es|-}} and {{bor|en|NL.|Bolivia||[[land]] of [[Bolivar]]}}, from the South American revolutionary leader {{w|Simón Bolívar}} + {{m|la|-ia||''[[form]]ing [[placename]]s''}}, from the {{der|en|es|-}} surname {{m|es|Bolívar}}, from {{der|en|eu|Bolibar}}, a village in [[Álava]], [[Basque Country]], [[Spain]], from {{der|en|eu|bolu||[[windmill]]}} + {{m|eu|ibar||[[valley]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/bə.ˈlɪv.i.ə/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/boʊ.ˈlɪv.i.ə/|/bə.ˈlɪv.i.ə/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-Bolivia.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪviə|s=4}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q750}}{{place|en|country|cont/South America|capital=La Paz|capital2=Sucre|official=Plurinational State of Bolivia}}.
# {{place|en|small town/county seat|co/Brunswick County|s/North Carolina|c/USA}}.
# {{lb|en|historical}} {{former name of|en|Santa Cruz|nodot=1}}, {{place|en|island|p/Galapagos|c/Ecuador|a=an}}.

